  "claim_boundary": "This development-only protocol is authorized by the completed dynamic collection-prefix gate and reuses the already-observed source-v4 public plan, unqualified development reader, and theta0 v2. Before any forecast is invoked it writes and fsyncs one content-addressed parent index containing 112 root-local eight-entry schedules derived only from public root and decision positions. Each synthetic root executes collection exactly once, with four onboarding sessions and decisions zero through seven carried through exact owner persistence. The current preaction is fsynced before the admitted source owner opens the actual forced-action branch; PE-derived credit is settled without online gate mutation. The resulting eight exposures and credits form one batch for that root only. Three fresh gates share the exact batch plan: full APPLY, frozen_theta0 WITHHOLD, and strict_noop the same canonical WITHHOLD receipt. Full is recoverable only from theta0 plus the exact batch and APPLY receipt; all future arms start from the same opaque terminal owner persistence bytes. The natural dynamic trace, its outcomes, and its credits are never read. PASS authorizes freezing a separate forty-decision development campaign protocol only. It does not authorize campaign or evaluation execution, estimate an arm or ability effect, qualify the reader, establish unseen or formal evidence, Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable, four-able completion, human evidence, or production ACTIVE. The 112 roots are synthetic operational units, not people, and source-v4 action-specific randomness is not a common-random-number design. No reader rehearsal, model invocation, or CUDA execution belongs to this protocol."
